Generated from [prodij/copio](https://github.com/prodij/copio). Update with `copier update --trust`.

    make env          # writes .env (git-ignored) with generated local secrets
    make up           # starts the stack
    make bootstrap    # configures Zitadel, Lago and (with a key) Stripe; safe to run again
    open http://{{ domain }}:5173    # 5173 is the default APP_PORT; use yours if you changed it

Stripe is optional. Without a key you can sign up, create a workspace and use the app, but billing
isn't set up: `POST /billing/checkout` answers 501 with that message, Billing says so, and paid features
stay off (`require_feature` still answers 402). To add it, paste a Stripe TEST secret key (sk_test_ only,
not rk_test_: https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/apikeys) into `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=` in `.env` and run
`make bootstrap` again. `make up` alone is not enough: it gives the backend the key, but Lago has no
Stripe provider until `make bootstrap` adds it, and new workspaces fail until then. Workspaces created
before the key get their Stripe customer at their first checkout.

## Mock payment (local tests with no Stripe account)

Mock payment fakes only the payment step, so `make e2e` can prove sign-up to premium with no Stripe key.
It is off by default. To turn it on, keep `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` empty, set `BILLING_MODE=mock` and
`APP_ENV=local` in `.env`, then `make up && make bootstrap && make e2e`.

- The backend won't start, and `make bootstrap` stops, with `BILLING_MODE=mock` and any other `APP_ENV`, with a
  Stripe key set, or (bootstrap) while Lago still has a Stripe provider. No request can turn it on.
- Real Zitadel, real Lago and Lago's real signed webhook stay in the path. Lago gets a subscription with no
  payment rule and no provider, makes it active and sends `subscription.started`. Coming back to the app grants
  nothing: `require_feature` answers 402 until that webhook lands. Stripe is never called and `stripe-cli` stays idle.
- The app shows a "Mock payment" banner on every page. Lago's invoice stays unpaid, because nothing pays it.
- **A mock payment pass is not a Stripe pass.** The Stripe payment test is reported as skipped. The mock run does
  not prove Stripe's page, saved cards, Lago's payment-gated subscription, or what happens when a payment fails.
- `billing_reconcile` still asks Lago every 15 minutes, and Lago says active, so a lost webhook is repaired
  there as usual. That is why the test stops the job while it checks that only the webhook grants access.
- Leaving mock payment: `make reset`. A subscription it made stays active otherwise, and Lago still has it.

Host ports are set in `.env` (defaults: app 5173, API 8000, Zitadel 8085, its login page 3100,
Lago API 3000 and UI 8088, Postgres 5432, S3 (SeaweedFS) 8333). Change any that clash with another
project, then `make up`. Every port is published on 127.0.0.1 only.

- `make e2e` runs the Playwright tests against the running stack (after `make bootstrap`): sign-up to
  `/plans` always, sign-up to premium when `.env` has a Stripe key (reported as skipped without one), and
  sign-up to premium by mock payment when `.env` has `BILLING_MODE=mock`. `make check` runs lint, types and unit tests (needs Postgres: `make up`).
- Brand colours, font and logo live in `brand/brand.yaml`; they reach the app, the Zitadel login
  page and Lago when `make brand` runs (`make bootstrap` runs it too).
- The Zitadel console (`http://auth.{{ domain }}:8085/ui/console`, with your ZITADEL_PORT) signs in
  as `admin@{{ domain }}` with `ZITADEL_ADMIN_PASSWORD` from `.env`; the Lago UI as
  `LAGO_ORG_USER_EMAIL` with `LAGO_ORG_USER_PASSWORD`.
- `make doctor` lists stuck workspaces, checkouts and webhooks; `make reset` deletes all local data.
